  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 226 AM EST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nA brief period of mid/upper level ridging is expected early to\nmid-week, with low-level easterly flow continuing around the\nsurface ridge. This will likely keep us from completely drying out\nthrough early next week. However, by mid-week, a frontal system\nmoving through the central CONUS is forecast to start pushing the\nlow-level ridge northeastward. This will give us a more southerly\ncomponent to the low-level winds and end the persistent shower\nactivity. It'll still be humid, just not as wet. There is a ton of\nmodel divergence on how that central CONUS system evolves, but it\nseems like the majority of the solutions bring a pretty weak\nfrontal boundary through Florida by the end of the week.",
